I've finally got around to implementing my old idea of different kinds
of poisoned weapons: sleep, confusion and paralysis. The patch is
available from my nethack web-page [1].

In summary, you can now dip poisonable weapons into potions of sleep,
confusion and paralysis and get a coating of the corresponding type,
with the appropriate effects. I also applied this to other cases where
poisoned weapons are generated, like dart traps.

There still is one bug I can't track down. When you dip into an
unknown potion of the appropriate type you should get a weapon with an
unknown coating type, but for some reason the coating is known. If
anyone can spot the bug, let me know.

This patch should not affect save-game compatibility. Existing
poisoned weapons should remain poisoned. Save games and bones files
can probably also be transferred in from the patched version to the
unpatched version without incident also, although coated weapons in
the patched version will become poisoned in the unpatched. Still, I
haven't tested this, so tread carefully.

